Centralised Logging Management System: Automated Apache Log Collection via Jenkins
Overview
To support the xFusionCorp Industries DevOps team in maintaining and analyzing server logs across the Nautilus infrastructure, this project implements a periodic, automated Jenkins CI/CD pipeline (copy-logs). The job securely collects Apache web server logs (access_log and error_log) from Application Server 1 (stapp01) and archives them centrally onto the Storage Server (ststor01) under /usr/src/finance.

Architecture & Workflow
[ Application Server 1 (stapp01) ] 
       │
       ▼ (Secure SCP via sshpass using credentials)
[ Jenkins Server (copy-logs Job) ] 
       │ (Scheduled every 10 minutes: */10 * * * *)
       ▼
[ Storage Server (ststor01) ] ──> Target Directory: /usr/src/finance
Jenkins Job Configuration Details
1. Build Trigger (Schedule)
Configuration: Build periodically

Cron Expression: */10 * * * * (Executes automatically every 10 minutes).

2. Build Step (Execute shell)
The pipeline runs the following shell commands to pull logs securely and transfer them to central storage:

Bash
# Create a temporary working directory locally on the Jenkins runner
mkdir -p /tmp/apache_logs

# Copy Apache access_log and error_log from stapp01
# User: tony | Password: Ir0nM@n
sshpass -p 'Ir0nM@n' scp -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no tony@stapp01:/var/log/httpd/*_log /tmp/apache_logs/

# Transfer the collected logs to the Storage Server (ststor01)
# User: natasha | Password: Bl@kW | Destination: /usr/src/finance
sshpass -p 'Bl@kW' scp -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no /tmp/apache_logs/*_log natasha@ststor01:/usr/src/finance/
